# carts/digger — scripted walkthrough of the cave. Play it with:
#
#     quarp replay record carts/digger -o carts/digger/replays/walkthrough.qrpr \
#         --ticks 768 --input-file carts/digger/replays/walkthrough.input
#
# Grammar (quarp replay record --input-file): tick:buttons, entries separated by commas or
# newlines, '#' starts a comment. Buttons are L R U D O X S; an empty list releases
# everything, and what is named on a tick stays held until the next entry.
#
# The cave advances one grid step every 6 ticks and a step uses the direction held on
# that tick, so a whole run of steps is one entry: "5:D" is held from tick 6, which is
# step 1. Nothing here is a tap: this cartridge reads Btn, not Btnp, and latches the last
# direction seen since the previous step.
#
# What happens when — every line below was read back out of the cartridge itself, tick by
# tick, not just planned:
#
#   tick   54   the boulder at (9,1) loses its floor and comes loose
#   tick   60   it drops into (9,2), one step behind the digger
#   tick   66   it lands in (9,2) and thuds
#   tick   78   he walks back into it and shoves it west into (8,2)
#   tick  150   gem 1 of 5, at (20,1)
#   tick  216   the boulder at (30,1) loses its floor and comes loose
#   tick  222   it drops into (30,2), one step behind the digger
#   tick  228   it lands in (30,2) and thuds
#   tick  312   gem 2 of 5, at (16,4)
#   tick  348   gem 3 of 5, at (15,9)
#   tick  528   gem 4 of 5, at (5,15)
#   tick  696   gem 5 of 5, at (27,21)
#   tick  696   quota met: the exit at (38,22) unlocks
#   tick  768   he steps into the open exit at (38,22) — LEVEL CLEAR
#
# 128 steps, 768 ticks, 5 of 7 gems, two left in the cave on purpose.
5:D,11:R,71:L,83:R,149:U,155:D,161:R,221:L,299:D,311:L,323:D,353:R,383:D,
413:L,419:D,437:L,497:U,509:L,533:R,557:D,569:R,635:D,659:R,767:D,768:
